- recent correlated failures;
- cache/disk/GC;
- RCC local/provider/cache-service state where applicable;
- redaction manifest.

## Acceptance

1. zero-config local install starts, autoreloads, executes via bundled RCC, and survives restart without external services.
2. local mode can optionally use one promoted non-RCC adapter without making it fallback.
3. simple production runs two Runtime replicas, PostgreSQL, and independent workers without sticky routing/broker.
4. RCC provider/`cache serve` can be added for environment distribution but Runtime remains correct without it for local/warm cases.
5. health/readiness distinguish process, DB, provider, adapter compatibility, real proof, worker, and capacity failure.
6. graceful drain/upgrade preserves pinned Runs/Attempts/Runtime Plans and rejects stale writes.
7. mixed coordinator/worker/adapter/provider versions pass declared matrix or fail closed.
8. backup/restore recreates authoritative state/content and verifies immutable identities.
9. air-gapped install executes preseeded Package and selected runtime content.
10. configured shared backend/provider/adapter never silently falls back.
11. single-/multi-Workspace isolation evidence exists.
12. container/Kubernetes placement introduces no semantic behavior unavailable to ordinary process contracts.
13. adapter shadow→enforce promotion is exact-subject, auditable, and rollback-safe.

## Non-goals

- Building a hosted proprietary Control Room/SaaS.
- Requiring Kubernetes/operator/service mesh/broker.
- One pod/server per package.
- Agent conversation/model lifecycle.
- General cloud infrastructure provisioning.
- Treating local caches as authoritative by default.
- Reimplementing RCC cache/provider/backup internals.
- Automatic adapter fallback.
- Shipping every conceivable adapter without demand/reopening criteria.

